    "text": "Connection Termination > Any of the two parties (client or server) can close the connection, although usually initiated by client. Two options for connection termination: > Three-way handshaking _> four-way handshaking with a half-close option Three-Way Handshaking: Step-1: > Client TCP, after receiving a close command from client process, sends a FIN segment in which the FIN flag 1s set. > FIN segment can include last chunk of data sent by the client, or it can be just a control segment. > If itis only a control segment(does not carry data), it consumes only one sequence number.",
